       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "size": 1,
        "text": ""
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "title": "How the look is decided",
        "variant": "quiet",
        "pad": [
         2,
         1
        ],
        "text": "A screen never names a colour. It asks for a <b>variant</> (card, quiet, hero, alert) and a <b>tone</> (accent, warn, pos…).\nThe theme answers: its <b>tokens</> are the colours, its <b>parts</> style what the runtime draws (headers, the selected row,\nborders, the caret), its <b>variants</> are named looks. Themes are the person's, loaded with <accent>fictty run --themes</>;\na push never changes them. Press <accent+b>t</> and watch every screen in this showcase change at once.",
        "size": 8
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "col",
      "children": [
       {
        "type": "input",
        "id": "g_input",
        "bind": "g_input",
        "title": "input",
        "size": 3,
        "pad": 1,
        "placeholder": "A one-line field. Type here; Enter does whatever the screen says."
       },
       {
        "type": "row",
        "children": [
         {
          "type": "editor",
          "id": "g_editor",
          "bind": "g_scratch",
          "title": "editor",
          "pad": [
           2,
           1
          ],
          "text": "A caretline editor on the store entry `g_scratch`.\n\nSelect with Shift and the arrows, undo with Ctrl-Z.\nOpen this chapter twice: the text is where you left it.\n",
          "syntax": "markdown"
         },
         {
          "type": "text",
          "size": 1,
          "text": ""
         },
         {
          "type": "editor",
          "id": "g_mirror",
          "bind": "g_scratch",
          "title": "the same entry, another editor",
          "variant": "quiet",
          "pad": [
           2,
           1
          ],
          "syntax": "markdown"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
